{{also|Feminist}}
==English==

===Etymology===
First recorded in English 1852. Ultimately from {{der|en|la|fēminīnus}}, from {{m|la|fēmina|t=woman}}. See also {{m|en|feminine}}, {{m|en|feminism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɛmənɪst/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|fem|in|ist}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# relating to or in accordance with [[feminism]].
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|date=2000-05-01
|author={{w|bell hooks}}
|title={{w|Feminist Theory: From Margin to Center}}
|edition=2nd
|page=xi
|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=uvIQbop4cdsC&pg=PR11
|passage='''Feminist''' struggle takes place anytime anywhere any female or male resists sexism, sexist exploitation, and oppression.
}}
#: {{hypernyms|en|egalitarian}}

